://t.co/6ZRzc8BKLD","type":"STRING"},"summary_photo_image_original":{"image_value":{"height":1080,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/card_img/2109162229388189696/LGzxhoU6?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1920},"type":"IMAGE"}}},"isEdited":false,"isStaleEdit":false}},{"tweet_id":"2108860261897584940","text":"here's how to build a game like this with Claude Opus 5.5 + Blender + Unity 6...\n\nthe trick is preparing everything before Opus writes a single line, but there's a smart way to set it up:\n\n- step 1: connect Claude Code to Unity and Blender through MCP\n- step 2: write one big brief: the world, the mechanics, the UI, the mood, plus reference images\n- step 3: add a CLAUDE.md with your rules, and design docs as the single source of truth so Opus never guesses\n- step 4: split the work into subagents: design, modeling, textures, and one reviewer that only looks and approves\n- step 5: Opus models the assets in Blender: the island, palms, pier, boat, fishing hut\n- step 6: it builds a greybox in Unity first, plays it, fixes it, and repeats\n- step 7: mechanics one layer at a time: walking, casting, bait, catching, day and night\n- step 8: you watch and give feedback with a reason: \"too dark at dusk\", \"cut the water stripes\"\n\nand the two rules that make it work...\n\nthe agent that builds is never the one that approves\nevery fix gets written into a file, so the next project starts smarter\n\nstart small, a fishing game is the perfect first project","username":"rewind02","tweet_url":"https://x.com/rewind02/status/2108860261897584940","first_link":"https://x.com/rewind02/status/2108860261897584940/video/1","created_at":"October 10, 2026 at 07:00PM","liked_at":"2026-10-11T00:01:41.041565","source":"ifttt","private":false,"notfound":false,"react_tweet_data":{"__typename":"Tweet","favorite_count":1320,"lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"created_at":"2026-10-10T10:00:41.000Z","display_text_range":[0,275],"entities":{"media":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/WZZ3Sqt1Q8","expa